# START (0.16.26): the next power-on comes back to the piece last played (once it has played 20 s), exactly as stored; Random (the Settings page's Start)
# is the old way. A test boot (seed 0) is always the first piece, so the other scenarios are unchanged.
seed 0
seamless 1
wait 3000
expect genre 0
expect piece 0
press GLO
wait 100
turn PRESET 2
wait 200
release GLO
wait 300
turn PRESET 3
wait 300
expect genre 2
expect piece 3
# not yet 20 s on it: a power-on now would not know it
wait 21000
# a real power-on (seed not 0): back to HOUSE 04
seed 7
reboot
wait 2500
expect genre 2
expect piece 3
expect saved 0
# the settings walk: HOLD HOME opens SETTINGS (its first page); the fourth knob is Start: Random
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 200
spin K4 1
wait 6000
seed 7
reboot
wait 2500
expect genre 0
